id: pm-u3o3ur
title: "GH-931: linked-test detector misclassifies unrelated node dist/cli.js commands as pm"
description: "The linked-test execution classifier treats any Node script ending in dist/cli.js as the pm CLI, so unrelated project commands receive false PM context, mismatch, and sandbox diagnostics."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-08-07T19:42:35.002Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-07T19:47:13.723Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 150
acceptance_criteria: PM command detection proves executable identity instead of matching a generic dist/cli.js suffix; actual pm binary package and checkout invocations remain recognized; unrelated Node CLIs remain non-PM with and without leading environment assignments; execution-context and mismatch receipts stay accurate across CLI and SDK tests.
parent: pm-e97jyf
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: high
environment: @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.7 linked-test runner in a non-pm consuming project
repro_steps: "Link node dist/cli.js schema research --format json with pm test --add-json, run pm test ITEM --run, and observe execution_context.is_pm_command=true plus mismatch_detected=true for the unrelated executable; repeat with a leading environment assignment."
expected_result: Only an executable whose pm identity is established receives PM execution context; generic project dist/cli.js commands remain ordinary linked tests.
actual_result: The 2026.8.7 suffix heuristic marks every node path ending in dist/cli.js as pm and emits false mismatch metadata.
customer_impact: "Ordinary project tests are mislabeled and can be failed or rerouted by PM context enforcement, undermining the trustworthiness of linked verification evidence."
